# the_gap_03 — TERRAIN, NOT MASONRY
#
# BACKLOG A2.  ⚠ This is the SOURCE; `maps/the_gap_03.json` +
# `maps/the_gap_03_markers.json` beside it are BUILT from it by
# `scripts/build_maps.sh` and are what `make play MAP=the_gap_03` loads.
# `tests/a2_the_maps.loft` asserts the two still agree.
#
# ⚠ It is also playable directly, without building:
#     make play SCRIPT=maps/the_gap_03.keys
#
# ⚠⚠ A map holds the GROUND and the MARKERS and nothing else.  A `crew`
# or a `schedule` line here would be authored, played, and then silently
# dropped by the save — the run's wave list is the seven-wave default
# every `PlayState` starts with (`waves.loft::wave_list_default`).
#
# A rock massif with one gap in it.  Nothing here can be repaired and
# nothing here can be broken — the perimeter is the ground itself.
# ⚠ The strongest base the repo can build today: WAVE 5 (`@M045`).
echo the_gap_03: a massif with one gap in it, and the rock never breaks

at 0 0 1

palette 5

# The home field, west of the massif.
drag   -6  -8    5  -8
drag   -6  -7    5  -7
drag   -6  -6    5  -6
drag   -6  -5    5  -5
drag   -6  -4    5  -4
drag   -6  -3    5  -3
drag   -6  -2    5  -2
drag   -6  -1    5  -1
drag   -6   0    5   0
drag   -6   1    5   1
drag   -6   2    5   2
drag   -6   3    5   3
drag   -6   4    5   4
drag   -6   5    5   5
drag   -6   6    5   6
drag   -6   7    5   7
drag   -6   8    5   8

# The approach, east of it.
drag    9  -8   23  -8
drag    9  -7   23  -7
drag    9  -6   23  -6
drag    9  -5   23  -5
drag    9  -4   23  -4
drag    9  -3   23  -3
drag    9  -2   23  -2
drag    9  -1   23  -1
drag    9   0   23   0
drag    9   1   23   1
drag    9   2   23   2
drag    9   3   23   3
drag    9   4   23   4
drag    9   5   23   5
drag    9   6   23   6
drag    9   7   23   7
drag    9   8   23   8

# ── The massif: three hexes deep, right across the map. ──
#
# ⚠⚠ `steep_rock` carries `walk_ground = false` and is NOT a structure,
# so `structure_breakable` answers false: a robot can neither stand on
# it nor ever chew through it.  starter_01's `wall` is 3 m of masonry
# with HP and it comes down.
#
# ⚠ It stops the VEHICLE too — measured, not assumed.  `walk_vehicle` is
# true for all twelve palette kinds and NOTHING READS IT yet
# (`src/passable.loft` § walk_ground is NOT passability), so the rock is
# no more passable to the player than to the robots.  The gap is the
# only way through for anybody, in either direction.
palette 8
drag    6  -8    8  -8
drag    6  -7    8  -7
drag    6  -6    8  -6
drag    6  -5    8  -5
drag    6  -4    8  -4
drag    6  -3    8  -3
drag    6  -2    8  -2
drag    6  -1    8  -1
drag    6   0    8   0
drag    6   1    8   1
drag    6   2    8   2
drag    6   3    8   3
drag    6   4    8   4
drag    6   5    8   5
drag    6   6    8   6
drag    6   7    8   7
drag    6   8    8   8

# ── And the gap cut back through it, three hexes wide. ──
#
# ⚠ Three rather than one on DRIVING grounds, not on defensive ones:
# swept from 1 to 11 hexes wide, the width is worth 2 ticks in 233
# (`@M045`) — the wallet's drain saturates at the core's own footprint,
# so throttling the approach buys nothing today.
palette 5
drag    6  -1    8  -1
drag    6   0    8   0
drag    6   1    8   1

# ── The markers ──
do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click    0   0
marker   0   0 target

# FOUR towers around the mouth of the gap.
#
# ⚠⚠ Two is the WORST of one, two and four — measured, and it is not a
# repair artefact, because it reproduces with the player left out at the
# spawn.  Towers kill, kills leave BODIES, and bodies are terrain
# (`docs/ENEMY_MOVEMENT.md` § Bodies are terrain): two guns kill fast
# enough to choke their own kill zone and not fast enough to win anyway.
# Four out-shoot the problem — 110 shots against 39 — and this is the
# only base in the repo that reaches WAVE 5.
do cycle_kind
click    2   0
click    4   0
click    2  -1
click    2   1
marker   2   0 tower
marker   2   1 tower

# The spawn, 21 out — past the forward tower at (4, 0) plus its 15.
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click   21   0
marker  21   0 spawn 3

do toggle_mode

count markers 6 6
kind 0 0 grass
kind 7 0 grass
kind 7 4 steep_rock
kind 7 -4 steep_rock
